      "1": {
        "citation": "Although both Douay-Rheims and pinned Swete expose fifteen numeric verses in Nahum 1, Douay 1:15 includes the concluding idea 'he is utterly cut off'; pinned Swete continues that conclusion in source 2:1 ('Συντετέλεσται, ἐξῆρται') after its 1:15 good-tidings/festival text. Numeric equality therefore does not prove complete verse-boundary identity."
      }
    }
